# LibreWolf rs-blocker-android.patch  (Android)
# Owner: LW-M4-08 ("Apply the remote-settings blocker to the Android build")
#
# THE DEFECT
# ----------
# A first-run capture of an APK with all 13 Android patches applied still shows
# 3 Remote Settings hosts, 14 events, with real TLS:
#
#   firefox.settings.services.mozilla.com
#   firefox-settings-attachments.cdn.mozilla.net
#   content-signature-2.cdn.mozilla.net
#
# Desktop's fix (patches/rs-blocker.patch, in common.txt) touches only the
# JS/Gecko stack: services/settings/*.mjs + SearchEngineSelector.sys.mjs.
# Fenix's Remote Settings traffic goes through the RUST RemoteSettingsService
# in third_party/application-services/components/remote_settings/, which the
# desktop patch never reaches. librewolf.services.settings.allowedCollections
# (settings/common.cfg:698) is inert for the collections Fenix actually syncs.
#
# THE FIX
# -------
# Three hunks in the Rust crate, closing all network choke points:
#
#   1. service.rs  fetch_changes()  -> return empty Changes (no network)
#   2. client.rs   sync()           -> no-op (no network)
#   3. client.rs   make_request()   -> return error (block all remaining egress)
#
# The server stays Prod, so is_prod_server() remains true and the packaged
# data path (get_records Case 1, get_attachment step 2, reset_storage re-seed)
# keeps working. The seven packaged collections (regions, search-config-v2,
# search-config-icons, search-telemetry-v2, summarizer-models-config,
# translations-models, translations-wasm) and their attachments are served
# from the binary. search-config-overrides-v2 is NOT packaged, but Fenix
# passes applyEngineOverrides=false (SearchEngineSelectorRepository.kt:60-62),
# so no client is ever created for it and nothing reads it.
#
# What this does NOT do:
#   - Does NOT change the server URL (Custom would disable packaged dumps
#     via the is_prod_server() gate at client.rs:715-721 - strictly worse).
#   - Does NOT remove the RemoteSettingsService or its Kotlin wrappers -
#     the offline read path (get_records(false)) still works.
#   - Does NOT touch the JS/Gecko Remote Settings (already covered by
#     rs-blocker.patch in common.txt).
#
# SCOPE / ORDERING
# ----------------
# Touches two files in third_party/application-services/components/remote_settings/:
#   - src/service.rs
#   - src/client.rs
# No other patch in either list touches these files. No ordering constraint.

